From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ninjacornix <milanvrankic@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:36:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(editor): new-project wizard says less and shows more
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Joinery-only, not for upstream. Every step: a three-dot stepper beside the title replaces "Step N of 3", and the footer's summary shows only on the step that creates, collapsed to "73 files · MIT · downloads GodotSteam ›" (pressed, it reads in full). Step 1: the starting points come first, as 16:9 pictures with their names (the pitch is the tooltip); the folder is one line, shortened in the middle, with a Change… link; the pitch's reason is its tooltip. Step 2: each feature is its name, a one-line caption from the CLI and its switch, with the summary and what it adds in the tooltip; Steam asks only for its app ID ("Add later") and, with online play, a Steam/Direct segmented control. Step 3 is "The look", marked Optional: one drop zone that becomes a three-column grid of pictures with what to take from each typed under it, five palette swatches (chosen, or picked from the pictures) that answer the palette question as hex values, and a refusal that names the file and fades after four seconds. The reference and document files, notes and answers written to the project keep their format.
